-- Seed public.kanji + public.kanji_components (issue 13 — QA humaine)
--
-- Root cause: public.kanji had exactly 1 row (一) in the live Neon DB —
-- the import:kanjidic2 / import:kradfile pipeline (scripts/import/) was
-- never run against it. public.cards.kanji_id references public.kanji, so
-- completeLesson() threw cards_kanji_id_fkey for every kanji except 一 —
-- i.e. nearly every real lesson — surfaced to players as the generic
-- "セーブできませんでした" (could not save) screen at the end of a lesson.
--
-- Generated by a one-off script (scripts/build/_tmp_generate_kanji_seed.mjs,
-- not committed) from:
--   - src/data/kanji-content.json (id/meanings/on/kun/jlpt/grade/etymology/mnemonic)
--   - scripts/sources/kanjidic2.xml.gz (stroke_count, matched by literal)
--   - unicode_hex derived from the character codepoint
--   - scripts/sources/kradfile + kradfile2 (kanji_components edges, both ends
--     restricted to the 2136-kanji Jōyō set; component_ids on kanji itself is
--     left at its schema default of '[]', matching scripts/import/import-kanjidic2.ts
--     — no existing pipeline script populates that column either)
--
-- Idempotent: `on conflict do nothing` throughout, safe to re-run.
--
-- Apply with: npm run db:migrate -- db/migrations/008_seed_kanji.sql

on conflict (id) do nothing;

on conflict (parent_id, component_id, source) do nothing;
